    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The U.S. military continues to enhance its capabilities through technological advancements and deployments. The Navy&#39;s USS Abraham Lincoln has returned to Naval Base Guam, marking a return from a deployment that included a stop in the South China Sea. The USS Savannah (LCS-28) fired a SM-6 missile, demonstrating its operational capabilities. The U.S. Navy is seeking to deploy containerized low-cost interceptors to defeat cruise missiles and attack drones. The Marine Corps tested an Unmanned Surface Vessel equipped with integrated autonomous driving and payloads for littoral operations. The Army promoted sergeants to staff sergeants upon completion of the Drill Sergeant Course. The Army&#39;s POW/MIA recognition day honors former prisoners of war and those still missing in action. The Army&#39;s merit-based promotions authority enables the merit-based promotion of eligible sergeants to master sergeants, with a follow-on lateral promotion. The Army&#39;s medical professional received a doctoral scholarship for her work in nutrition and diet therapy. The DCMA&#39;s 9/11 Commemoration shares Stephanie Sturdevant&#39;s personal story of how the events of 9/11 shaped her life. The Marine Corps&#39; Drill Sergeant Course commander, Col. Brogan Issitt, was recognized for his distinguished leadership. The DLA Distribution San Joaquin Commander&#39;s recognition highlights the importance of leadership in the military.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
  </Document>
